put an auto-reply asking the sender to resend their message to
'sensors@'.

BTW- I use 'spambouncer' scripts to tag messages.  It does a pretty 
good job (about 90% accurate).  It automaticly blocks knows virii, but 
only tags and lets through spam.  You can see if it has been tagged as 
likely spam by looking for this in the header:

X-SBClass: Blocked

I'd block everything which has that except there are still a number of 
mails it tags this way which are still legit.


